## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design of data contracts, lineage, and governance in a multi-domain Azure data mesh, with real ingestion patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Data contracts across domains
- End-to-end lineage with Purview
- Delta Lake schema evolution and time travel
- Domain isolation via access controls
- Canary tests for contract changes

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo contract test for incoming record
function validateContract(record, contract) {
  // contract = {schema: {...}, required: [...], checks: [...]}
  if (!contract.required.every(k => k in record)) return false;
  // simple type checks
  for (let key of Object.keys(contract.schema)) {
    if (typeof record[key] !== contract.schema[key]) return false;
  }
  // custom checks
  return contract.checks.every(fn => fn(record));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you version contracts and rollback a breaking change?
- How would you monitor contract violations and auto-generate lineage dashboards?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design decisions for a unified real-time and batch ingestion platform, data governance, schema management, late data handling, and cross-service upserts in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Delta Live Tables, Delta Lake, Purview lineage, MERGE upserts
- Event-time processing, watermarks, late data handling
- Ingest from Azure Event Hubs and on-prem SFTP into ADLS Gen2
- Synapse Analytics star schema load and Delta Lake schema evolution
- Artifact layout, lineage tagging, cost-aware orchestration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-schema validation for streaming records
function validate(record, schema) {
  const required = schema.required || [];
  const missing = required.filter(k => !(k in record));
  if (missing.length) throw new Error("Missing fields: " + missing.join(", "));
  if (schema.types) {
    for (const [k, t] of Object.entries(schema.types)) {
      if (typeof record[k] !== t) throw new Error("Invalid type for " + k);
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test and prove end-to-end lineage across Purview for both streaming and batch paths?
- What strategies would you employ to handle evolving schemas with zero downtime?
